{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:FluidDynamics.P2CriticalExponent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"FluidDynamics.P2CriticalExponent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent.enstrophy_diverges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent.enstrophy_diverges","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p2-critical-exponent.lean#L77-L77","doc":"**The conjecture itself.**  The enstrophy diverges as $q \\to 1$:\non *every* punctured neighbourhood of $q = 1$ it exceeds every\nbound $M$.  This is the finite-time-blowup statement at the\nsubstrate-parameter level.\n\nThe `1 < q ∧ q - 1 < ε` conjunct localises the divergence at\n$q = 1$ and is essential: without it the field asserts only that\nenstrophy is unbounded somewhere, a condition satisfied by\n`enstrophy q = max q 0`, which is the identity near $q = 1$ and\nhence regular exactly where the conjecture asserts blow-up\n(counterexample verified in\n`docs/audits/2026-08-29-q-ns-conjecture-statement-strength-probe.lean`).\n\nThe neighbourhood is one-sided, matching the statement's\n$q \\to 1^{+}$ and the substrate regime $q > 1$.\n\nThe field asserts unboundedness on every right-neighbourhood of\n$1$, which is weaker than the accompanying asymptotic\n$\\Omega_{\\max}(q) \\sim (q-1)^{-\\alpha}$: the divergence *rate*\nis not encoded, and `criticalExponent` is accordingly\nunconstrained by any field of this class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent.enstrophy_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent.enstrophy_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p2-critical-exponent.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Enstrophy is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent.criticalExponent_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent.criticalExponent_pos","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p2-critical-exponent.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Critical exponent is positive (genuine divergence, not a\nbounded oscillation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent.criticalExponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent.criticalExponent","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p2-critical-exponent.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The critical exponent governing the asymptotic\n$\\mathrm{enstrophy}(q) \\sim |q-1|^{-\\gamma_c}$ as $q \\to 1$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent.enstrophy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent.enstrophy","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p2-critical-exponent.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Enstrophy of the flow at substrate parameter $q$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p2-critical-exponent.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.CriticalExponent","kind":"class","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p2-critical-exponent.lean#L38-L79","doc":"**`conj:critical-exponent` (axiomatised).**\n\nThe enstrophy of the $q$-NS flow blows up as $q \\to 1$ with a\nuniversal positive critical exponent.  The final field encodes the\nconjecture proper: enstrophy is unbounded on every punctured\nneighbourhood of $q = 1$. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:critical-exponent","label":"conj:critical-exponent","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p2-critical-exponent.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}